Package: kwaainet
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kwaai AI Lab <dev@kwaai.ai>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: ca-certificates
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://kwaai.ai
Description: node CLI for the KwaaiNet decentralized inference network
 KwaaiNet is a peer-to-peer network for sovereign AI: model inference and
 training run across machines contributed by their owners rather than inside a
 single provider's data centre. This package provides kwaainet, the command
 line tool that runs and controls a node on that network.
 .
 A node joins over libp2p through bootstrap peers, announces the transformer
 blocks it is able to serve, and finds other nodes through a distributed hash
 table. Large models are split block-wise across several nodes, so a machine
 too small to hold a model whole can still serve a slice of one and take part
 in distributed inference. Nodes behind NAT are reached by hole punching or
 relay circuits, so port forwarding is not normally required.
 .
 Also included is p2pd, the libp2p daemon the node runs alongside itself, and a
 systemd user unit. The unit is installed but not enabled: run
 "systemctl --user enable --now kwaainet" to start a node at login.
